{"content":[{"c":["AHINOAM"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Daughter of Ahimaaz and wife of King Saul (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.14.50","r":"1Sam.14.50","rawR":"1Sam.14.50","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.14.50","value":"1Sam.14.50"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 14:50"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Jezreelite woman who became David’s wife after Saul took back his daughter Michal and gave her to Palti (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.25.43-44","r":"1Sam.25.43-44","rawR":"1Sam.25.43-44","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.25.43-44","value":"1Sam.25.43-44"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 25:43-44"},"). In Hebron, Ahinoam became the mother of David’s oldest son, Amnon (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.3.2","r":"2Sam.3.2","rawR":"2Sam.3.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.3.2","value":"2Sam.3.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 3:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.3.1","r":"1Chr.3.1","rawR":"1Chr.3.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.3.1","value":"1Chr.3.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 3:1"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Ahinoam","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Sm 14:50","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.14.50","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.14.50","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.14.50"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 25:43-44","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.25.43-44","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.25.43-44","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.25.43-44"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 3:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.3.2","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.3.2","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.3.2"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 3:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.3.1","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.3.1","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.3.1"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"ee0a592a7bd30184543073abb17d47beb3dca606c1c1358b5db79fc3e6b471c4","sourceItemName":"Ahin